{
  "schema": "wuwa.rotations.v2",
  "_howToEdit": [
    "A rotation is: a team, an enemy, the buffs that are live, and an ordered list of steps.",
    "Steps may switch character freely — write the whole loop as one list, in the order you press things.",
    "",
    "  { \"char\": \"aemeath\", \"ability\": \"<exact label>\", \"count\": 1, \"note\": \"...\" }",
    "",
    "'ability' must match the label in ref/proj-<char>.json exactly. The runner page lists every",
    "valid label per character, and any typo shows up as a loud warning rather than a silent zero.",
    "",
    "'count' repeats the step. 'crit' can be \"average\" (default), \"noncrit\" or \"crit\".",
    "'raw' injects a fixed number instead of computing one — used for main-echo damage, which the",
    "character projection files do not carry.",
    "",
    "'buffs' lists buff ids from characters.json. A buff only reaches a character if it is",
    "target:'team' or owned by that character. Delete an id to test without it.",
    "",
    "enemy.res may be a single number (applied to every element) or an object per element."
  ],

